# Scheduled jobs for the stock-lakehouse stack.
#
# WHY CRON AND NOT THE `schedule` LIBRARY
# ----------------------------------------
# The `schedule` package runs inside a Python process that dies with the
# machine and is not supervised. This file is a real crontab, mounted into
# the `scheduler` container, which runs `cron -f`. The container has
# `restart: unless-stopped`, so the timetable survives a crash and a
# reboot of the host.
#
# WHY TWO TIMETABLES
# ------------------
# The two jobs serve different purposes and have different natural
# cadences:
#
#   * The EOD batch runs ONCE per market day, after that market closes.
#     Running it more often would re-fetch the whole universe for nothing.
#   * The two batch entries cover the two market closes. There is no
#     intraday job: the news poll was removed on 12/11/2026 together with
#     the whole news pipeline (see the removal notes below).
#   * The quality gate, the universe forecast and the walk-forward report
#     run ONCE per day, after both market closes, because all three of
#     them need the settled bars.
#
# THE TIMES ARE UTC
# -----------------
# The container's timezone is UTC (see the `scheduler` service in
# docker-compose.yml), so these times are UTC:
#
#   * NYSE closes at 20:00 UTC (16:00 America/New_York) in EDT, and at
#     21:00 UTC in EST. The batch runs at 21:30 UTC, which is after BOTH
#     closes - running at 20:30 would miss the last hour of every summer
#     session.
#   * HOSE closes at 07:45 UTC (14:45 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh). The batch runs
#     at 08:30 UTC (15:30 Vietnam time), allowing provider settlement.
#
# The symbols overlap in time, so both sessions are covered by two runs.
#
# WHY THE UNIVERSE FORECAST RUNS SEPARATELY, AND LATER
# ------------------------------------------------------
# The forecast pass does two things: it predicts the next session for every
# symbol, and it SCORES the forecasts whose session has already happened.
# Both need the price layers to be settled, so it cannot start before the
# EOD batch has finished for that market.
#
# It runs in the early morning UTC because that is after the HOSE batch
# (08:30 UTC) and before the NYSE close, and the forecast it publishes
# covers the NYSE session that is about to open. The scoring part then
# verifies the previous day's forecasts against the closes that have
# happened.
#
# The gap between the two jobs is deliberate: the forecast pass needs the
# settled bars, not the mid-session snapshot.
#
# The jobs are logged to /app/logs/scheduled_jobs.log, which is the record
# of what actually ran.

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
APP_HOME=/app

# ── End-of-day batch (price layers + next-session forecast) ────────────────
# NYSE: 21:30 UTC (after the 20:00/21:00 UTC close)
30 21 * * 1-5 root cd $APP_HOME && /opt/venv/bin/python scripts/run_scheduled_job.py eod >> $APP_HOME/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# HOSE: 08:30 UTC (after the 07:45 UTC close)
30 8 * * 1-5 root cd $APP_HOME && /opt/venv/bin/python scripts/run_scheduled_job.py eod >> $APP_HOME/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ── Universe forecast (predict every symbol + score the old forecasts) ─────
# 09:30 UTC: after the HOSE batch has settled the bars, before the NYSE
# session opens. The forecast it publishes covers the coming NYSE session.
#
# WHY ALL THREE MODEL FAMILIES
# ----------------------------
# The pass publishes one forecast row per (symbol, model, target_session), and
# the table's unique key is exactly that triple - so the three families
# coexist without a schema change. A symbol that has no trained model for a
# family gets NO row for that family; it never receives a substitute forecast.
#
# What is published per family therefore depends on what has actually been
# trained: `linear_regression` covers the whole universe (~1.002 symbols),
# while `arima` and `lstm` cover the representative liquid sample across 14
# exchanges (58 symbols). The comparison table on /forecast therefore shows
# three columns for the sampled symbols and one for the rest - which is the
# honest picture, not a gap.
#
# Measured cost of the whole pass after the LSTM inference fix (17/11/2026,
# all three families, whole universe): 2.76 minutes of inference.
30 9 * * 1-5 root cd $APP_HOME && /opt/venv/bin/python scripts/run_scheduled_job.py universe-forecast --model linear_regression,arima,lstm --no-train >> $APP_HOME/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ── Data quality gate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 10:30 UTC: after both EOD batches and after the forecast pass, so the
# gate checks the layers as they are LEFT by the nightly work.
#
# The gate is the only job that makes a network call to the provider, so it
# runs on its own and its own failure cannot stall the price refresh. Its
# provider comparison rotates over the universe, so each run checks a slice
# and a full sweep completes over many runs.
30 10 * * 1-5 root cd $APP_HOME && /opt/venv/bin/python scripts/run_scheduled_job.py quality-gate >> $APP_HOME/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# ── Multi-symbol walk-forward report ────────────────────────────────────────
# 22:30 UTC: an hour after the NYSE end-of-day batch has settled the
# bars, and clear of the forecast pass (09:30) and the quality gate
# (10:30), so this CPU-bound job does not compete with them.
#
# WHY IT RUNS EVERY NIGHTDAY
# --------------------------
# The report used to be a hand-written snapshot: a file that somebody
# produced once, and that nothing ever refreshed. The numbers on the
# Backtesting page were therefore whatever was true on the day the file
# was written, with nothing on the page saying so.
#
# This job is the fix. It runs the SAME machinery the manual script runs
# - the shared service, so the two cannot drift apart - and writes the
# result into the lakehouse's `backtests` layer. That layer is MinIO in
# production, which is the one place the `scheduler` container and the
# `backend` container can both reach: they do NOT share the `data`
# volume, so a file written to the scheduler's filesystem would be
# invisible to the API.
#
# The report covers the strategy layer's central claim - does the
# strategy beat simply holding the stock, across many symbols, on
# PAIRED windows? - so it has to be current for that claim to be
# defensible.
#
# Measured cost: 102 symbols over ~37 windows each took 75.5 s on
# 18/11/2026 for the MA-crossover report. Two strategies are run, so
# the pass takes a few minutes.
30 22 * * 1-5 root cd $APP_HOME && /opt/venv/bin/python scripts/run_scheduled_job.py walk-forward --strategy ma_crossover,rsi_strategy --per-exchange 8 >> $APP_HOME/logs/cron.log 2>&1

